scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: firefly
run_id: 1
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 10
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No tests or implementation distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors in from_file_or_default. Config loading tests cover TOML loading and env
    overrides but no evidence of error-type discrimination.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA explicitly lists ''CWE-209: Error Display doesn''t leak internal
    paths/stack traces'' as a security test in cli_error_exit_codes.rs. Dev passed
    all 134 tests, so implementation must satisfy these constraints.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA lists ''Header injection: CRLF in tenant ID and auth token rejected/sanitized''
    in siem_client.rs tests and Dev mentions ''header injection prevention''. However,
    the deeper type-safety issue (using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core)
    is not addressed.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Cargo.toml changes show +2 additions for uuid and chrono as direct dependencies.
    No mention of workspace = true convention enforcement anywhere in the pipeline.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: "TEA says 'Token field in TOML file is ignored (OS keychain only)' \u2014\
    \ this encodes silent ignoring as correct behavior, which IS the vulnerability.\
    \ No test for deny_unknown_fields or warning on unrecognized fields. Dev says\
    \ 'token rejection' but the broader unknown-field issue is unaddressed."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). This is a bug in TEA's own test output that passed through dev and review
    uncaught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config). This is
    a bug in TEA's own test output that passed through dev and review uncaught.
